            <ArticleTitle>Management of celiac artery aneurysm: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>609-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of CAA in a 68-year-old male patient is reported. The patient had vague abdominal pain for 1 year. Physical examination revealed a pulsatile abdominal mass on the epigastrium. Abdominal ultrasonography and visceral arteriography confirmed the diagnosis of CAA. Aneurysmectomy with direct implantation was performed transabdominally.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
